WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.558 --> 00:00:01.674
[gun fires]

00:00:01.674 --> 00:00:04.064
[tires squeal]

00:00:04.064 --> 00:00:05.610
I'm not going to say
it doesn't ever happen,

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.360
but not very often.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.260
And we don't drive a lot of Ferraris.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.270
My name's Andy Kay.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.936
I'm a private investigator,

00:00:11.936 --> 00:00:14.670
and I'm also the owner of Kay
and Associates Investigations

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.002
here in Los Angeles for
about the last 30 years.

00:00:17.002 --> 00:00:18.735
Today I'm going to be looking

00:00:18.735 --> 00:00:20.670
at private-investigator scenes

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.337
from movies and television.

00:00:26.418 --> 00:00:27.630
What do you want?

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.072
HDS, sir. And how are you this afternoon?

00:00:30.072 --> 00:00:31.270
All righty, then.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.780
I've been a delivery
guy a couple of times.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.090
I've been a waiter.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.777
I've actually asked a maître d' to give me

00:00:39.777 --> 00:00:42.568
the bottle of wine to deliver
to the table one time.

00:00:42.568 --> 00:00:44.270
So, yeah, it happens.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:47.220
There's actually laws against
impersonating another person.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.529
Walking up with the outfit,

00:00:49.529 --> 00:00:51.070
nobody's going to say anything about it.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:51.997
If you go up there and say,

00:00:51.997 --> 00:00:53.730
"Hey, I am FedEx,"

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.713
then you're stepping over a line.

00:00:59.661 --> 00:01:01.998
Son of a b----!

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.250
Ace: That was a close
one, ladies and gentlemen.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.860
When little animals go missing,

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.780
unless we have good information

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.660
that somebody has stolen
it or it's a big dog,

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.470
expectations are pretty low.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.251
It happens, and we've gotten some back.

00:01:15.251 --> 00:01:17.120
Nobody's going to do it like that,

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.210
because you would not know, first off,

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.961
that the dog was going
to be anywhere accessible

00:01:20.961 --> 00:01:22.180
in the first place,

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.686
that the guy is going
to even answer the door

00:01:23.686 --> 00:01:24.980
in the second place.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.610
There is just so much
presumption in this case

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.023
that it would just never happen that way.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:32.826
Except for Jim Carrey.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:33.810
[engine sputters]

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.450
No problem! It gets flooded.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:36.758
We'll just wait a few seconds.

00:01:36.758 --> 00:01:37.950
[man yells]
[glass shatters]

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.033
All that planning just to be caught

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.799
at the end with a baseball bat. [laughs]

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:44.340
Usually we don't have
to worry about getaway.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.383
The big thing about being
a private investigator

00:01:46.383 --> 00:01:47.340
is to be private,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.300
so that they don't ever
know we were there.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.070
I would give this clip a 2.

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:54.183
It's designed to be comedic,
and it's very good at it.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.530
Sherlock: Ah, sergeant, we haven't met.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.855
Dimmock: Yeah, I know who you are.

00:01:58.855 --> 00:02:00.013
And I'd prefer it if you didn't

00:02:00.013 --> 00:02:02.620
tamper with any of the evidence.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.578
The police officer,
first thing he said was,

00:02:04.578 --> 00:02:06.940
"I prefer you not be
disturbing our evidence,"

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.750
and that's exactly correct.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.590
They would have never
let him in those doors

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.023
at that point. Once they were there,

00:02:13.023 --> 00:02:14.300
they would have taken over the scene.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.340
The disdain for what he was saying

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:18.740
shows you that they are not big fans

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:19.810
of private investigators,

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.090
which is a lot of the times

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.720
the situation with police officers.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.680
A lot of times we are
working with the police,

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.730
a lot of times we are
working against the police.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.810
Left-handed?

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:29.830
I'm amazed you didn't notice.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.420
All you have to do is
look around this flat.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.820
Coffee table on the left-hand side.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.387
Coffee mug handle pointing to the left.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.520
Power sockets, habitually he
used the ones on the left.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.210
You can notice things
that are out of sync.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.080
I mean, that's extreme, for sure.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.330
And all that's going to come
out in pathology anyway.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.500
They're going to know if
he's right- or left-handed.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.870
There should be dozens and dozens

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:49.660
of photos of the crime scene.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.490
So they're going to notice
some of those things.

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:53.472
There's nothing there
that wouldn't come out

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.550
through the normal process anyway.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.720
And the private investigator's

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.843
not going to be a part of that.

00:02:58.843 --> 00:03:00.350
There's a lot of different things

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.740
you can tell about people
from looking at them

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:03.850
and appearance-wise,

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.010
but if you start assuming too much,

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:09.790
you might've fallen into a trap
for what they're, you know,

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.360
trying to make themself be portrayed as.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:17.270
So, you look. You don't
draw conclusions that way.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:21.636
I would rate that at probably a 5,

00:03:21.636 --> 00:03:22.910
just because it's entertaining

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.543
and you have to make it such,

00:03:25.543 --> 00:03:27.233
otherwise it's not going to work.

00:03:29.048 --> 00:03:30.578
[phone dials]

00:03:30.578 --> 00:03:33.264
[phone rings]

00:03:34.105 --> 00:03:35.465
Hi, this is Gia.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.537
Well, there's a whole
lot of violations of law

00:03:39.537 --> 00:03:40.370
in this one.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.920
We have this thing called
expectation of privacy

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.330
that we're supposed to work within.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:50.130
And so if you can see
something from public view,

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:53.670
without magnifying it, you can record it.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:57.280
If you can hear a conversation in public,

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.080
again, the expectation of privacy is gone.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.840
So you can do that.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.310
Taping phone calls,
it's a two-party state.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.770
It's in California, obviously.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.200
They said they're in West Hollywood.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.260
So you cannot record that phone call.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.030
If she was licensed, she
wouldn't be for much longer

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.520
if she was caught doing it.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.400
You can get the information other ways.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.270
And you definitely couldn't use it

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:21.430
in any kind of a court or a prosecution,

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.120
because they're going to toss it all out.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.391
So it's worthless for anything other than

00:04:25.391 --> 00:04:29.050
developing corroboration with
other evidence that you find.

00:04:30.805 --> 00:04:33.489
Gia: Hey, something's happening.

00:04:33.489 --> 00:04:35.771
You need to get over here right away.

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:39.040
I've had situations like this

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.600
where we actually just
rented the apartment

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:42.433
across the street.

00:04:42.433 --> 00:04:45.190
That way, if I can open my
window and see into theirs,

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.720
it's fair game.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:51.680
So there's ways around what she's doing.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.600
And this is, obviously,

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.180
an area where she wouldn't expect anybody

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.730
to be looking in on her.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.570
Although if people have
public access to that roof,

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.730
she could also be in the same situation.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:02.947
Say it's a rooftop bar

00:05:02.947 --> 00:05:04.910
and she's just sitting there at a table.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.968
She has the right if she can see it.

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:08.468
I have to get a closer look.

00:05:08.468 --> 00:05:10.930
Yes, sometimes cameras do come in handy.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:14.214
Now there's much smaller magnifications

00:05:14.214 --> 00:05:17.211
that we use that do the same job.

00:05:17.211 --> 00:05:20.870
We also use drones a
lot with magnification,

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.170
because if we can see it from there,

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.660
we can get anywhere on it.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:26.740
If it's in public space,
we can magnify on it.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.690
I'll give this clip two stars,

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:32.830
just because it's absolutely nothing

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:35.260
a private investigator is going to do.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:38.992
Did you converse with Harlan at that time?

00:05:38.992 --> 00:05:41.020
Well, he was there, we must have spoke.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.755
In his study?

00:05:44.669 --> 00:05:45.830
I don't think so.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.160
From an interrogation standpoint,

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.710
it was actually pretty good.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:52.640
He left information out of the question

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:54.810
so that they could try
to extrapolate on it,

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.180
and that way you can see
which way they're going.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.905
You could see that Don Johnson

00:05:58.905 --> 00:06:01.405
was coached a little bit on how to react

00:06:01.405 --> 00:06:03.040
while you're trying to hide something

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.060
and you're trying to
convey something else.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.470
So it was done well.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.746
Just the way he led his expressions

00:06:09.746 --> 00:06:10.858
and then, "Oh, yeah,"

00:06:10.858 --> 00:06:12.560
you know, kind of
things. Things like that.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.340
The things that you look for are

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:16.631
when they look away a lot,

00:06:16.631 --> 00:06:19.006
when they have to stumble,

00:06:19.006 --> 00:06:21.900
when they say things that
are just out of line anyway.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.810
They try to divert from something

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:25.280
when you ask a question.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.243
Now, a lot of people will hang their hat

00:06:28.243 --> 00:06:30.547
off of watching some ex-FBI agent

00:06:30.547 --> 00:06:32.040
tell you how to read people.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.770
And once you do that, you
start missing everything else.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.250
You really have to trust yourself

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.260
and your interactions with people.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:41.471
So you really have to pay
attention to those body cues

00:06:41.471 --> 00:06:44.740
and facial cues without becoming a victim

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:48.690
of counting on every single
one to mean a certain thing.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.280
Who hired you?

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.828
I do not know.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:55.790
An envelope of cash showed
up at my apartment yesterday

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.130
with a news clipping of Thrombey's death.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.420
Well, actually just today we got a case

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.710
where we have an anonymous client.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:04.070
I know she's a female.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.500
That's all I really know about her.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:09.240
So it's very strange,
but, yeah, it happens.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.850
You really want to know
who your clients are

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.310
the majority of the time.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:14.535
I give it ...

00:07:14.535 --> 00:07:15.568
7.

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.750
One of the more realistic
portrayals so far.

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:20.700
What makes you certain

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:25.180
that your husband is
involved with someone?

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:26.780
A wife can tell.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.613
Good scene.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:29.150
Now, as I recall, in this movie,

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.540
that was not the actual person

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:33.140
she was portraying herself to be.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.920
But she was right about that statement.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:39.010
When she said, "A woman knows
these things," she was right.

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:39.870
Women know.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:43.152
We actually keep the numbers every year,

00:07:43.152 --> 00:07:45.790
'cause we do a lot of these
cases all over the globe.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:49.278
It's always between 96% and 99%

00:07:49.278 --> 00:07:51.840
of the women that hire us are right.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.310
Guys are about 50%.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.920
They know about half the time

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.020
if it's really happening or not.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:02.840
They just tend to be more
wary of other men around

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:04.270
or things like that.

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:06.853
So it's about 50% with guys,

00:08:06.853 --> 00:08:09.503
about 96% to 99% with women.

00:08:09.503 --> 00:08:10.940
One of the big giveaways

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:13.410
is being overprotective of the cellphones

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.870
and the pads and any
of their other devices.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.020
We've got a great
digital-forensics department.

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:20.580
Somebody brings us a
computer or a telephone,

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:23.400
we can retrieve, you know,

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.670
deleted texts, deleted pictures,
all those kind of things.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:30.740
Mrs. Mulwray, this type of investigation

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.610
can be hard on your pocketbook.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.400
It takes time.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.320
Money doesn't matter to me, Mr. Gittes.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.100
Most investigations are expensive.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:41.480
It's not a cheap thing to get into.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:44.373
For infidelity cases, I've had cases go

00:08:44.373 --> 00:08:47.730
where we were watching somebody 24/7

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.800
for three weeks.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.227
And I got on the phone
with my client, and I said,

00:08:52.227 --> 00:08:54.820
"Hey, he's not doing what
you think he's doing."

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:57.600
And she says, "Andy, please stay on this.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.040
I know."

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.537
And so we did, and, honestly,

00:09:00.537 --> 00:09:04.160
it wasn't two days later before he was at

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.560
one of the high-end
hotels in Beverly Hills

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.153
with two prostitutes.

00:09:08.153 --> 00:09:09.645
And then three days later,

00:09:09.645 --> 00:09:12.552
we end up at a townhouse up in Agoura

00:09:12.552 --> 00:09:14.070
where he paid for it

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.020
and he's had a woman living there with him

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:19.030
for years that nobody knew anything about.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.300
So sometimes it takes a long time.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.200
I would rate the accuracy of this scene

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.441
a 10 out of 10.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:35.550
Following people on foot,

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.440
you definitely want to do
a lot of the things he did.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:38.440
Stay out of sight,

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.710
don't look ridiculous enough
to everybody else around you

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:42.270
that they're saying,
"Hey, there's a guy, like,

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:45.040
hiding behind the wall watching
you go around corners."

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:45.890
You don't want to do that.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:47.960
You always have to look
just like you belong there,

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:49.380
because it's not just that person

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.620
you have to worry about seeing you.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:52.280
You have everybody else

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:55.420
that if you're acting
weird and stalkerish,

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:57.170
they're gonna go tell somebody.

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:58.636
Last thing you want to do
if you're following somebody

00:09:58.636 --> 00:09:59.560
is have the police pull you over

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:00.810
to ask you what you're doing.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.400
That kind of ends the
surveillance right there.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:05.606
Quite often when we end
up in a on-foot situation

00:10:05.606 --> 00:10:06.830
where we're doing a surveillance,

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.720
it started off in a vehicle.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.240
So you don't know

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:12.840
exactly what you're
going to be able to do,

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.391
and like I talked about in
some of the other situations,

00:10:15.391 --> 00:10:17.899
you have to be able to flow
with it as things change.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.600
Almost all my guys, when
they're doing surveillance,

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.500
they'll have a couple extra shirts or tops

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.130
or maybe a pair of shorts.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:28.130
Anything that they can switch out fast

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:30.290
to make themselves look different

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.710
and not catch the eye over
and over and over again.

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:34.120
Because if they're walking in an area

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:36.250
where there's not a lot
of people for a long time,

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:38.730
a lot of people take walks
in parks, things like that.

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:41.463
So you have to kind of
be ready to be on foot.

00:10:46.772 --> 00:10:48.170
It wasn't terrible.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:51.820
You want your disguise
not to be so ridiculous

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:53.530
that it's noticed as ridiculous,

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.930
because then they're going
to pay attention to you.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:58.360
His was a little over the top there.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:02.492
I'd give him a 7. 8. We'll go 8.

00:11:02.492 --> 00:11:03.489
[gun fires]

00:11:03.489 --> 00:11:06.090
[tires squeal]

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:07.270
The biggest misconception

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.380
people have about private investigators

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:11.420
is that we're always in gunfights

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.200
and that we're out arresting people.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:16.620
And that's not very often what happens.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.190
I'm not going to say
it doesn't ever happen,

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.320
but not very often.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.090
And we don't drive a lot of Ferraris.

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:24.023
I would give this clip a 2.

00:11:32.485 --> 00:11:34.890
In that scene, it's much
better than watching

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:37.700
the subject of the
investigation being followed

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:40.520
by a red Ferrari half
a car length behind him

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:41.360
and not noticing it.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:43.430
If you can't be out of sight, blend in.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:47.460
You want to use cars
that fit in everywhere.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:50.790
I mean, we use a lot of
Priuses in Los Angeles.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.270
The other thing is,

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:53.998
anytime you're following somebody

00:11:53.998 --> 00:11:55.779
and you end up in a situation

00:11:55.779 --> 00:11:57.392
where you're in a lot of traffic,

00:11:57.392 --> 00:11:59.993
odds are they're going
to take a lot of turns,

00:11:59.993 --> 00:12:01.130
things like that.

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:04.870
Of course, use a very inconspicuous car

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.500
and also try to use several.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:09.460
That way somebody can leapfrog these.

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:11.560
We can have a car on the opposite way.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:12.393
And if they come

00:12:12.393 --> 00:12:14.547
and we know that this
one's going to take a left,

00:12:14.547 --> 00:12:15.720
"Hey, coming towards you."

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:18.020
Then you're already in the street over,

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:19.550
you pick up the car, you go off.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.060
The next one turns in behind

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:22.680
and then tries to leapfrog ahead.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.977
If we have to speed, we do it.

00:12:24.977 --> 00:12:25.810
It was amazing,

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:28.400
'cause he was actually
keeping an OK distance,

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:31.000
but there was never, ever
any traffic in between them.

00:12:39.228 --> 00:12:41.610
Woman parks, and he
stops right in the lane

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:42.640
and sits and watches her.

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:45.110
That's a sure way to be seen.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.910
So, not a good tail.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.670
If you think somebody is tailing you,

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:52.340
start making unnecessary turns

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.681
into places that are odd

00:12:54.681 --> 00:12:56.581
and then make multiple turns.

00:12:56.581 --> 00:12:58.710
Make them follow you into those turns.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:01.220
I'll give him 5, 'cause
I like Jimmy Stewart.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:03.760
Rust: I remember there
was no physical evidence

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:07.976
connecting Dora Lange to the
dude's place out in the woods,

00:13:07.976 --> 00:13:09.610
meaning it probably
didn't happen out there.

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:11.174
Yeah, it still happens a lot.

00:13:11.174 --> 00:13:13.170
We use a lot of big whiteboards

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:14.800
with a lot of drawings through in this,

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:16.910
and then a lot of those
get erased as we go.

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:19.540
And we have lots of mirrored rooms

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:21.950
that the same thing happens with dry erase

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.010
and we put pictures on so we can see them,

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:25.780
and as things develop and change,

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:29.420
most cases just don't need
that kind of investigation,

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:30.737
but we use it a lot.

00:13:40.447 --> 00:13:43.020
Rest of the family, they
don't really talk to Aunt D.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.100
There's a whole plethora
of things that we can do

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:46.450
that law enforcement can't do.

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:47.900
We can talk to people,

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:49.390
I don't have to read you your rights.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:52.342
I can start questioning
you from the beginning

00:13:52.342 --> 00:13:55.270
with the intent of
having you confess to me.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.642
Obviously, the biggest thing is

00:13:56.642 --> 00:13:58.860
I can go anywhere in the world and work,

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:01.250
and I don't have to let
anybody know I'm there.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:05.000
And we don't need to take a
ton of time for approvals.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.610
So, if you tell me

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:09.420
that you need to have
a certain thing done,

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:13.266
we can prioritize it because
you're paying us to do it,

00:14:13.266 --> 00:14:16.390
whereas law enforcement
may never prioritize it.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.090
So they may never get to it

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:19.850
just because they're overrun.

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.791
In that part he did
pretty good, I thought.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.710
In this scene, you've got a father

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:33.330
who's looking for a lost daughter.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.310
He's obviously very bereaved.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.670
I think he's doing the right
thing by going through this.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.870
I think this is a very common scene.

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:43.310
I think that a lot of people
do these types of things

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:45.519
when this happens, even
before they call us.

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:51.640
Social media, websites, places
where they have memberships,

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:53.100
things like that are always important

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:54.470
in those kind of investigations.

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:56.309
We employ them a lot.

00:15:05.455 --> 00:15:08.277
Some of the times you will use photographs

00:15:08.277 --> 00:15:10.350
and things and do reverse imaging.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:13.050
Now, I'm not talking about
doing a Google reverse image.

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:15.670
We use a lot of the
same soft- and hardware

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:19.250
that the FBI uses, that a
lot of law enforcement uses,

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.414
and it's only available

00:15:20.414 --> 00:15:22.770
to licensed investigators
or law enforcement.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.770
So we have very good people

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.936
that go and dig this stuff out.

00:15:27.936 --> 00:15:30.540
And a lot of times, if you
have a daughter that's missing

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:32.123
or a son that's missing,

00:15:32.123 --> 00:15:34.589
if we can have their computers,

00:15:34.589 --> 00:15:37.600
we can get a lot of information

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:39.630
about what their thought process was

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:40.990
before they ended up missing.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:44.090
There is no such thing as
secure on the internet. Nowhere.

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:45.560
If it can't be gotten right now,

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:48.358
it'll be available some other time.

00:15:48.358 --> 00:15:50.280
You just see what happened to Facebook,

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:52.240
where Mark Zuckerberg's phone numbers

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:54.640
and everything else ended
up hacked from his own site.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.540
So, nothing is safe.

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:57.670
I don't care who you are.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.620
I don't care what site it is.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:00.995
If you're putting it out there,

00:16:00.995 --> 00:16:01.911
you might as well expect

00:16:01.911 --> 00:16:04.670
that it's going to be
accessible to anyone.

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:06.536
So, at some point,

00:16:06.536 --> 00:16:08.502
if the right person wants to get in there

00:16:08.502 --> 00:16:12.040
and dig long and hard enough
and invest whatever it is,

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.736
time or money, they're going to find it.

00:16:13.736 --> 00:16:15.200
I would give this a 10 out of 10.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.945
It's a very accurate depiction
of what would happen.

